WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Hello everyone, and welcome. My name is Parth Pawar, and today I am excited to present my data analytics project:

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Analysing Mental Health in the Student Ecosystem. As higher education demands intense academic dedication,

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:22.000
understanding student well-being, everyday lifestyle habits, and autonomic biological stress has never been more critical.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:30.000
In this demonstration, I will walk you through the end-to-end analytical workflow, from dataset verification to interactive Tableau BI.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:38.000
In contemporary universities, mental health challenges such as chronic stress and anxiety frequently go unnoticed

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:46.000
until a student experiences acute academic burnout or severe absenteeism. Academic advisors lack unified diagnostic visibility.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:54.000
The core objective of this project is to build an interactive, data-driven BI platform bridging behavioral metrics, biomarkers, and grades.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Our analysis is powered by a verified dataset comprising exactly 1,000 collegiate profiles across 16 multi-dimensional variables.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:12.000
These span demographics, psychological ratings, sleep and study hours, attendance, LMS scores, Heart Rate Variability, and risk tiers.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:21.000
We conducted rigorous validation, confirming 100% data completeness with zero missing values and zero duplicate records.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:30.000
To prepare this dataset for Tableau, we engineered custom calculated fields for age groups and study intensity tiers.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Now, let us examine the published interactive Tableau dashboard, featuring an executive KPI scorecard and six core analytical views.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Our KPI scorecards summarize the cohort: average stress 5.45, average depression 5.50, and average nightly sleep 6.49 hours.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:02:00.000
In our study hours analysis, moderate study of 3 to 5.5 hours delivers optimal performance without triggering severe stress.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:10.000
Crucially, in our physiological view, students experiencing severe distress show significantly suppressed heart rate variability below 50 ms.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:20.000
Finally, our Mental Health Risk distribution reveals that 23.9% of students fall into the high-risk category requiring support.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:30.000
From our empirical findings, sleep duration serves as a powerful natural stress buffer, and social interaction mitigates depressive symptoms.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:40.000
To make these findings accessible, I developed a responsive portfolio web application deployed via GitHub Pages and GitHub Actions.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:50.000
In conclusion, this project illustrates how business intelligence transforms campus health data into actionable institutional insights.
